From cdac313edf39dc9a22c3a2f757c02996d5581295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:21:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: hostless modem voice through q6apm

Boards with modem voice graphs get private links copied from the physical
backends; the voice driver opens them to power codecs, clocks and
SoundWire while the DSP moves the call audio. q6apm-dai splits into the
DAI driver and the voice frontend, backend and PCM. APR and SoundWire stop
racing port removal and failed opens.

[cherry picked from 7c8cc30d7fc4; kept the SCM buffer assignment, S32_LE
playback, the ring wrap fix and the position buffer mask. q6apm_free_fragments
stays in compr_free. 5fd1171da118 is not needed: 195d048f6e41 does the same.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
